[size=5][b]Alan Wake Collectibles[/b][/size]
[b]For the original Alan Wake (2010), NOT Alan Wake Remastered.[/b] Tested only with the Steam version, on Windows and on Linux (Steam Deck).

The statistics screen only gives game-wide totals. This mod shows [b]what you still have to find in each episode and chapter[/b].

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]In-game overlay[/b]: found / total for your current chapter and its episode, updated as you pick things up.
[*][b]Menu counts[/b]: each episode and chapter shows what is left, per type.
[*]Manuscript pages, coffee thermoses, can pyramids, chests, radio shows, TV shows, signs, and both special episodes (alarm clocks, cardboard cutouts, video games).
[*]Nightmare-only manuscript pages counted separately.
[*]Hotkeys (F8 overlay, F9 menu counts) and a settings file for position, keys and text size.
[*]No game file is replaced, and nothing is sent anywhere.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]In Steam, right-click Alan Wake, then Manage, then Browse local files.
[*]If there is already a d3d9.dll there (from another mod, such as ReShade), rename it to [b]d3d9_next.dll[/b]. This mod will load it.
[*]Copy [b]d3d9.dll[/b] from the archive into that folder, next to AlanWake.exe.
[*]Start the game as usual.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Uninstallation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Delete d3d9.dll, alanwake_collectibles.ini and alanwake_collectibles.log from the game folder.
[*]If you renamed another mod's file to d3d9_next.dll, rename it back to d3d9.dll.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]The original Alan Wake (2010) only.[/b] Not for Alan Wake Remastered or American Nightmare.
[*]Tested only with the Steam version, on Windows and on Linux (Steam Deck).
[*]GOG and Epic versions are not supported.
[*]Menu counts need the Steam executable dated 2020-05-15; on others they switch off by themselves.
[*]The mod's text is in English, whatever the game's language.
[*]The small menu text was aligned at 2560x1440. If it looks off line on your screen, set menu_small_text=0 and let me know.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Good to know[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]"Current chapter" is the chapter of your last checkpoint.
[*]With small text, the mouse and the selection highlight cover the episode or chapter name only.
[*]An antivirus may flag the DLL, as it may any DLL that hooks into a game.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Changelog[/b][/size]
[b]0.7.1[/b] First public release.
